  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IOM Winterization Activities in Ukraine</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Additional grant to IOM&#x2019;s Winter Response Plan as part of the UN Winter Response Plan for Ukraine (October 2023-March 2024) coordinated by OCHA. IOM&#x2019;s plan targets 2 million people directly and 1,2 million indirectly, as well as 581 collective centres across Ukraine through activities such as shelter support (including solid fuel for institutions, house repairs and emergency shelter items), provision of winter NFIs, WASH (including infrastructure repairs during/after energy blackout and provision of mobile boilers and co-generation units), winterization of health facilities, psychosocial support, assistance in rural areas, support to collective centres as well as key data and analysis.

Gender equality and protection is at the core of the UN Winter Response Plan for Ukraine, as is also the case for the overarching 2023 Humanitarian Response Plan. Humanitarian partners commit to enhancing accountibility to affected people (AAP), preventing sexual exploitation and abuse (PSEA), increasing information and communication about conflict-related sexual violence and human trafficking, ensuring the response is gender-and age-sensitive, and promoting protection through all aspects of humanitarian programmes and advocacy. The reporting requires data disaggregated by sex, age, and disability.</narrative>
  </description>
